Chapter: ApproxStorageProbe
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 Probe for the Real approximate storage intrinsics: device-load-approx and
 device-store-approx move an f32 element (ld.global.f32, st.global.f32);
 test-approx-storage.ps1 asserts both forms and that the arithmetic between them is f32.

Section: Kernels

  gpu-approx-sq : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  gpu-approx-sq (xs) (out) (n) = act
   tid <- thread-idx-x
   if tid < n then approx-sq-one xs out tid
   else 0
  end

  approx-sq-one : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  approx-sq-one (xs) (out) (tid) = act
   v <- device-load-approx xs tid
   device-store-approx out tid (v * v + v)
  end

  gpu-approx-const : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  gpu-approx-const (xs) (out) (n) = act
   tid <- thread-idx-x
   if tid < n then approx-const-one xs out tid
   else 0
  end

  approx-const-one : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  approx-const-one (xs) (out) (tid) = act
   v <- device-load-approx xs tid
   device-store-approx out tid (v * bits-to-real-approx #BF000000 + real-approx-from-int 3)
  end
